3:# Avatar
4:Atlas Avatar v1 — identity image, initials or person icon, with optional status dot and badge icon. 3 types × 5 sizes × 2 shapes (30 total).
5-
6-USE WHEN
7-· Showing a person or entity beside a name in a list row, comment, header or member list.
8:· Showing a stack of members (AvatarGroup), optionally with an add button.
9-· Showing presence next to a person (showStatus).
10-DON'T USE WHEN
11-· The avatar must be pressed on its own → wrap it in Button.
12-· Showing a logo or product/content picture → Image.
13-· Showing a count or a text label → Badge.
14-HOW TO USE
--
18:· Use AvatarGroup for stacks; give it an aria-label. Pass size/shape on the group, not on each member.
19-· Default shape is circle; use squircle only for non-person entities (teams, orgs) if the design calls for it.
20-DO
21-· Keep initials to 1-2 characters.
22-· Match size to the adjacent text (xs-sm in dense rows, lg-xl in profile headers).
23-DON'T
24:· Attach onClick to an Avatar; it has no interactive states.
25-· Mix sizes or shapes inside one group.
26-RELATED
27:· Image — Avatar is identity with fallbacks; Image is a ratio-locked picture.
28:· Badge — Avatar identifies who; Badge labels or counts.
29-
30:Fallback order: valid image → initials → person icon. Alt text: an informative avatar (no adjacent name) gets meaningful alt text; a decorative avatar beside a visible name gets empty alt (alt=""); a failed image falls back to initials, then to the icon. Status dot uses the success token by default (swap the Status instance to change it) and is never colour-only — expose it as text to assistive tech. Shape=squircle uses the avatar-squircle-radius-* tokens. Avatar is presentational: no hover, active or disabled state.
